() Tj T*
(1. LT power cables shall be XLPE insulated 1.1 kV grade armoured cables with aluminium) Tj T*
(conductors as per IS 7098 \(Part 1\):1988.) Tj T*
(2. Size of the incoming feeder cable shall be 3.5 core x 300 sq mm.) Tj T*
(3. Continuous conductor operating temperature of XLPE cables shall be 90 Deg.C.) Tj T*
(4. Copper control cables of 2.5 sq mm shall be PVC insulated heavy duty type as per IS) Tj T*
(1554 \(Part 1\).) Tj T*
(5. Cable conductors shall meet the resistance requirements of IS 8130 for class 2) Tj T*
(conductors. Cables shall be laid directly in ground at a depth of 750 mm. with brick) Tj T*
(protection.) Tj T*
(6. Terminations shall be made with brass double compression glands and tinned copper) Tj T*
(lugs. Cable drums shall carry marking of size, type, length and manufacturer's name.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6 TESTS AND INSPECTION) Tj T*
(1. Performance tests on each pump shall be conducted as per IS 9137 in the presence of) Tj T*
(the Engineer.) Tj T*
(2. Pumps shall carry the BIS Standard Mark.) Tj T*
(3. Each motor shall be subjected to routine tests in accordance with IS 4029.) Tj T*
(4. Acceptance tests on cables shall be carried out as per IS 10810 in presence of the) Tj T*
(Engineer.) Tj T*
(5. Manufacturer's test certificates shall accompany every cable drum supplied. Pre-) Tj T*
(dispatch inspection shall be offered to the Department's authorised representative with) Tj T*
(15 days notice.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(7 DOCUMENTATION, WARRANTY AND TRAINING) Tj T*
(1. Shop drawings and schematic diagrams shall be got approved from the Engineer-in-) Tj T*
(charge before manufacture. O&M manuals, as-built drawings and catalogues shall be) Tj T*
(furnished in triplicate at the time of handing over.) Tj T*
(2. The supplier shall replace free of cost any part found defective within the defect) Tj T*
() Tj T*
